<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duchy of Westphalia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1180">1180</a>–<a href="/years/1816">1816</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> was a territory in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sauerland">Sauerland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnsberg">Arnsberg</a>. After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a> in 1180 it was granted to the archbishops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>, who ruled it until 1803. It was then given to Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> as compensation for lands lost to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and in 1816 it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duchy-of-westphalia.jpg" alt="Duchy of Westphalia" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NNW · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Herzogtum_Westfalen_und_Umland_etwa_1645.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
